  [OK] ... and it cannot conclude
  [OK] neither session is still open (one fulfilled, one revoked)

-- Scene 3: the question is a FRAME -- force opens it, slots fill it --
  [OK] with nothing known yet, the force is OPEN (:what)
  [OK] ... so no options are offered
  [OK] ... and the phrasing follows the force
  [OK] the frame names its slots + why
  [OK] once the domain KNOWS a value, the force closes to a choice (:which)
  [OK] ... the known value is OFFERED as an option
  [OK] ... the phrasing follows the new force
  [OK] ... and the option is NUMBERED in the text

-- Scene 4: REGISTER 1 -- answer an option by its number --
  [OK] a NUMBER picks the offered option
  [OK] the pick is really grounded in the space
  [OK] both known values are now on the table
  [OK] a LIST of numbers picks several options at once
  [OK] an out-of-range pick REFUSES -- it never guesses a value
  [OK] ... and the refusal reaches a human checkpoint

-- Scene 5: a checkpoint has a LIFETIME (it stops haunting) --
  [OK] the refusal is checkpointed
  [OK] by default a checkpoint NEVER expires (TTL 0)
  [OK] with a TTL, the stale checkpoint leaves the LIVE list
  [OK] ... but the audit record still holds it (nothing is deleted)
  [OK] ... and the expiry is reported
  [OK] a negative TTL REFUSES

-- Scene 6: FLUENCY upgrades honestly, or not at all --
  [OK] the deterministic floor is the default
  [OK] asking for neural fluency is recorded
  [OK] but the upgrade is only CLAIMED when a model is really loaded (LAW 3)
  [OK] an unknown fluency mode REFUSES

-- Scene 7: the checkpoint lifetime, across its RANGE and back again --
  [OK] TTL 0 never expires, however many turns pass
  [OK] TTL 1 expires on the first turn after
  [OK] TTL 2 survives that turn...
  [OK] ...and expires on the second
  [OK] TTL 3 survives two...
  [OK] ...and expires on the third
  [OK] with a TTL the checkpoint has left the live list
  [OK] ...and setting the TTL back to 0 brings it back
  [OK] ...with nothing expired any more
